/**
 * Oklahoma Basic Course of Real Estate, Part I of II (90 clock hours) — module question bank.
 *
 * 605:10-3-1(a)(1) lists TWENTY-TWO areas of study, (A) through (V), for the provisional sales
 * associate course, and allocates NO hours among them. So the topic list is the Commission's and the
 * module grouping, the hour allocation and the 80 percent engagement threshold are StateCourse
 * decisions for Commission review. Every module below records which of the twenty-two it carries, and
 * the engine holds the modules to covering all twenty-two.
 *
 * THE MOST IMPORTANT THING IN THIS FILE: Oklahoma abrogated common-law agency. 59 O.S. 858-360(A)
 * provides that the statutory duties "replace and abrogate the fiduciary or other duties of a broker
 * to a party based on common law principles of agency," and 858-360(B) that "a broker shall not be an
 * agent, subagent, or dual agent and an offer of subagency shall not be made to other brokers." No
 * item in this bank may treat Oklahoma as an agency state, and several items exist specifically to
 * catch a student who arrived with a national textbook's assumptions.
 *
 * THREE PASSING PERCENTAGES, THREE EXAMINATIONS, and an item that names one without naming its
 * examination would misstate the regulator:
 *   75%  the entity's end-of-course final examination      605:10-5-3(f)
 *   70%  the state provisional sales associate examination 605:10-3-5(f)
 *   80%  an instructor applicant's qualifying examination  605:10-5-1(f)
 * The 80 percent engagement threshold in THIS bank is none of those — it is a StateCourse standard for
 * in-module progression, which 605:10-5-3 does not prescribe.
 *
 * These items are NOT the end-of-course examination and are NOT a licensing examination. They gate
 * progression through a module and are visible to the student by design. Note that 605:10-5-3(e)
 * requires the end-of-course examination to consist of no less than 150 questions and provides that
 * "End-of-course examination questions may not be the same as any previously used questions covering
 * the respective course content" — so no item here may ever be used on that examination.
 *
 * Each module carries one applied item, five engagement items and five remediation items. The correct
 * answer is authored at index 0 and permuted deterministically per item id at delivery, so a recorded
 * selection keeps its meaning permanently. 605:10-5-3(i)(3) provides that "An answer key may not be
 * included in any course materials provided to the student" — the public delivery path strips
 * correctChoice and rationale, and a test proves it.
 *
 * Every Oklahoma section cited was read on 2026-08-20 from the Commission's Oklahoma Real Estate
 * License Code and Rules effective 1 November 2025, and is recorded in
 * oklahoma/regulatory/primary-text-readings.md. Where a source was NOT read — the Residential Property
 * Condition Disclosure Act, the Contract Form Committee's promulgated forms, 59 O.S. 858-208,
 * 858-301.1 and 858-4000.1, the deed theft notification form, the OREC syllabus, and Oklahoma's trust
 * account, foreclosure, landlord-tenant, probate, lien, tax, subdivision and mineral provisions — no
 * item asks a student to recall a figure from it. The authored answer is the routing.
 *
 * Course version 1.0 submission draft — not approved. No Oklahoma pre-license credit is available.
 */

