      { prompt: "Under § 858-355.1(E), what must a broker providing fewer services than a transaction requires disclose?", choices: ["In writing: a description of the steps in the transaction for which the broker will not provide brokerage services, and a statement that the broker assisting the other party is not required to provide assistance with those steps in any manner.", "Only that the services are limited.", "A reduced fee schedule reflecting the services omitted.", "Nothing, provided the brokerage agreement says the services are limited."], correctChoice: 0, rationale: "All three requirements must be met, and the third exists because the predictable harm of limited service is a party who assumes somebody will handle the gap. Note also what (E) permits: fewer SERVICES. It does not permit fewer DUTIES — § 858-353(A) and (B) are mandatory and unwaivable." }
